# The @Open-Transaction-Layer/maintainers team must exist in the organisation
# for this file to take effect, because GitHub silently ignores an owner that
# does not exist. It blocks a merge only while the main ruleset requires review
# from code owners.
*                       @Open-Transaction-Layer/maintainers

# Paths that decide what runs in CI, what gets installed and what gets
# published. They are listed explicitly so that a change to any of them is
# visibly a change to the supply chain, and so that the owner of these paths
# can be narrowed to a smaller security group independently of the rest.
/.github/               @Open-Transaction-Layer/maintainers
/scripts/               @Open-Transaction-Layer/maintainers
/.changeset/config.json @Open-Transaction-Layer/maintainers
/.npmrc                 @Open-Transaction-Layer/maintainers
/package.json           @Open-Transaction-Layer/maintainers
/package-lock.json      @Open-Transaction-Layer/maintainers
/packages/*/package.json @Open-Transaction-Layer/maintainers
/SECURITY.md            @Open-Transaction-Layer/maintainers
/LICENSE                @Open-Transaction-Layer/maintainers
/NOTICE                 @Open-Transaction-Layer/maintainers
